Ports Cabinet's file tree system into Multica as a self-contained KB
feature. All content is stored as markdown files on disk under
KB_DATA_DIR (default: ./kb-data) — no PostgreSQL required for KB content.

New files:
- apps/web/lib/kb/ — storage layer (path-utils, fs-operations, page-io,
  tree-builder) adapted from Cabinet, using KB_DATA_DIR env var
- apps/web/app/api/kb/ — Next.js route handlers for tree and CRUD
  (run before the /api/* → Go proxy rewrite)
- apps/web/stores/kb-tree-store.ts, kb-editor-store.ts — Zustand stores
- apps/web/components/kb/ — sidebar tree + editor shell UI
- apps/web/app/[workspaceSlug]/(dashboard)/kb/page.tsx — new route

Updated files:
- packages/core/paths/paths.ts — added kb() path
- packages/views/layout/app-sidebar.tsx — added Knowledge Base nav item
- packages/views/locales/en/layout.json, zh-Hans/layout.json — added kb label
- apps/web/package.json — added gray-matter and js-yaml deps
- .env.example — added KB_DATA_DIR variable
- README.md — added Knowledge Base section

