+## Knowledge Base
+
+Multica includes a built-in file-based knowledge base alongside its agent and task management UI. It uses the same markdown-on-disk approach as [Cabinet](https://github.com/hilash/cabinet) — no extra database, no separate service.
+
+### How it works
+
+- Pages are markdown files stored on disk under `KB_DATA_DIR` (default: `./kb-data` relative to `apps/web/`)
+- The sidebar shows a recursive file tree with drag-and-drop reordering
+- The editor is the same Tiptap WYSIWYG used across Multica
+- PDFs, CSVs, images, and diagrams render as first-class content types
+- Sub-pages nest inside parent directories (`parent/child/index.md`)
+
+### Access it
+
+Navigate to `/:workspaceSlug/kb` in the UI. A **Knowledge Base** link appears in the workspace sidebar navigation.
+
+### Configuration
+
+Set `KB_DATA_DIR` in your `.env` (or Docker Compose environment) to point at the directory where KB files should live:
+
+```env
+# File-based knowledge base data directory
+KB_DATA_DIR=./kb-data
+```
+
+The directory is created automatically on first use if it doesn't exist.
+
+### API routes
+
+The KB is served by Next.js route handlers at `/api/kb/` — these take priority over the `/api/*` → Go backend proxy rewrite, so no Go changes are needed:
+
+| Route | Method | Purpose |
+|-------|--------|---------|
+| `/api/kb/tree` | GET | Fetch the full file tree (supports `?showHidden=true`) |
+| `/api/kb/pages` | POST | Create a new page |
+| `/api/kb/pages/[...path]` | GET | Read a page's content and frontmatter |
+| `/api/kb/pages/[...path]` | PUT | Save content and frontmatter |
+| `/api/kb/pages/[...path]` | DELETE | Delete a page or directory |
+| `/api/kb/pages/[...path]` | PATCH | Move or rename a page |
+
+---
+
 ## Architecture
 
 ```
